how's it going everybody so I recently  saw venom and I must say going into it  hearing all the buzz about it hearing  some reviews say that it's really bad  hearing some say that it's really good  it is really confusing so today I'm  gonna give you my review of the movie  from my own perspective of course this  is just my own opinion and you should go  see it yourself and form your own I'm  going to try and avoid all potential  spoilers that I possibly can  I will however be talking about the  length of some scenes so if that is a  spoiler for you you have been warned and  if you're new to my channel be sure to  hit that subscribe button what the  notifications turned on so you can stay  up to date with all things relating to  venom marvel and so you can be entered  in my giveaway I'm giving away a few  copies of Avengers infinity war on  blu-ray some special edition posters and  memorabilia as well and congrats to  Tiffany Smith for being the next winner  of our giveaway email me and we'll get  you your prize so overall I thought  venom was a really great movie I'm  definitely going to be seeing it again  but having said that there are  definitely a few things that I would  change so let's talk a little bit about  the bat and then we'll end on the  positive the first thing is not  necessarily a bad thing to everybody but  for comic fans it probably is the movie  does not really stick to any story  relating to the comics although they did  a decent job with Eddie Brock's  character venom primarily revolves  around Spider Man I won't say whether or  not spider-man makes a cameo but this  movie is all about venom and Eddie Brock  venom doesn't even have the spider-man  logo on his chest like he always does in  the comics but if you keep an open mind  going into venom and accept a new origin  story you can get past that the next  thing is venom kinda starts off really  slow but it is a new origin story and  they have to set up each character and  they have to explain what the symbiotes  are so although necessary they could  have introduced the Venom symbiote a  little bit sooner another thing is that  the supporting cast is kind of just  there I didn't really develop any kind  of connection with them or  only care about any other character  besides venom and Eddie which is fine  because that's what the movie is about  the last thing I would mention is that  the final battle scene is very  anticlimactic and it's kind of short  don't get me wrong it is very very  awesome  and entertaining I just wish it could  have been a little bit longer so blowing  past all the tiny things that I would  change let's talk about how awesome the  movie is for starters Tom Hardy does an  excellent job he does a great job at  playing Eddie Brock and he does a great  job with a dynamic between venom and  Eddie this leads to not only a dark  movie but also a funny movie now I've  heard a lot of reviews that say the  venom movie couldn't decide which  direction to go dark and serious or  funny but I think that is the direction  they decided to go instead of having it  be one or the other  they went with both and in my personal  opinion it turned out very well you have  dark moments where venom wants to bite  the heads off everybody in a room and  then you have funny moments where Eddie  freaks out that venom slash himself eats  people which actually leads to the next  point and that is that the movie is  really hilarious there's a lot of humor  in the movie that is delivered really  well there are a few corny jokes in it  but again they are delivered pretty well  there's also a really good amount of  action in the movie when venom and Eddie  finally do bond you're on the edge of  your seat the whole entire time the  movie is packed with both action scenes  and hilarious scenes while  simultaneously being able to deliver a  serious tone I've heard that some people  think that it leans too much towards the  hilarious side but I actually think it  does a good job at managing the  hilarious side up with the dark side  with the serious side all at once  so overall it was a really good movie  that I very much enjoyed I was  entertained the whole entire time I  loved the action scenes  I love the comedy scenes and I loved the  fact that venom just wants to eat people  the whole entire time but again this is  just my opinion I highly encourage you  all to go see the movie for yourself and  form your own opinion  [Applause]  don't listen to a review that says the  movie is bad and not go see the movie if  you want to go see the movie go see it  I personally am going to see it again  and if you happen to go see it as well  come back here and let me know your  thoughts if you have seen it let me know  your thoughts in the comments below and  don't forget to subscribe like and  comment so you can stay up to date with  everything venom and Marvel related and  be entered in my giveaway as always  thank you all so much for watching  Wolf Wolf  [Music]
 

